    "video": {
      "name": "Keto Cheesy Bacon Ranch Chicken [with Cabbage Noodles]",
      "description": "Want to impress the family? Make them this amazing cheesy bacon ranch chicken dish, and you’ll be sure to make everybody happy. This tasty, yet keto-friendly dish includes lots of crowd-pleaser ingredients like bacon, cheese, and chicken. The good news is that it’s easy to make and can be cooked up in one pan.\n\nThe main protein source for this dish comes from juicy chicken thighs that get fried up in olive oil and smothered in a tasty mix of herbs and spices. Once the chicken is ready, you can add a bunch of rich and nutty mozzarella cheese to melt over the top (which is easily done by putting a lid over the pan). Once the cheese is melted, the last ingredient is some chopped-up cooked bacon to give the dish an even more amazing flavor profile.\n\nIf you’re not a fan of mozzarella, feel free to swap it out for any other melty cheese like parmesan or cheddar. Regardless of which cheese you use, it will add more depth to the dish, extra flavor, and more protein.\n\nThe final component of the dish is the chopped-up sautéed green cabbage, which you can quickly make in the same pan you cooked the chicken in. Once cooked, plate up the dish, sprinkle on some freshly cut chives, and get stuck in!\n\nRead the full recipe with full nutrition breakdown and step-by-step pictures over at:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIngredients:\n4 slice bacon\n200 gram green cabbage\n2 tablespoon olive oil\n10 ounce boneless, skinless chicken thighs\nSalt and pepper to taste\n1 teaspoon dried parsley\n3/4 teaspoon dried dill\n1/2 teaspoon garlic powder\n1/2 teaspoon onion powder\n3/4 cup shredded mozzarella\n2 tablespoon fresh chives, chopped\n\nNutrition Summary: This makes a total of 4 servings of Keto Cheesy Bacon Ranch Chicken. Each serving comes out to be 390 calories, 30.8g fat, 2.7g net carbs, and 25g protein.\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSee more keto recipes, knowledge and tips on the website to keep your weight loss going strong.\n\nEverything you need to know about the keto diet:\n\nGetting started? Everything you need is here:\n\nWe also make things easy with this 14 day diet plan:\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFollow Ruled.Me for more tasty food:",
